  {"date": "2023-10-10", "venue": "Ervin J. Nutter Center, Wright State University", "city": "Dayton", "state": "OH", "gap": 8, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Dark, brooding and sometimes searching, this is the epitome of latter-day Evil Phish Improv.", "out": "->", "prev": "It's Ice", "in": ">", "next": "Weekapaug Groove", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2024-04-20", "venue": "Sphere", "city": "Las Vegas", "state": "NV", "gap": 15, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "NYE's \"Bag\" casts a long shadow; fans of that momentous moment can turn from that script to find, here, more by way of impassioned (improvisational) play. Heavy as a multi-beast's footprints stomped into the Mojave's sand, the band toys with an array of effects to produce something like melody before Trey alights upon a line, a path leading the listener through a grassy path where one sees the forest for its cosmic trove of trees.", "prev": "Stash", "next": "Steam", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2024-07-19", "venue": "Xfinity Center", "city": "Mansfield", "state": "MA", "gap": 2, "set": "2", "out": ">", "prev": "Light", "in": ">", "next": "Beneath a Sea of Stars Part 1", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2024-08-02", "venue": "Ruoff Music Center", "city": "Noblesville", "state": "IN", "gap": 10, "set": "1", "out": ">", "prev": "Scent of a Mule", "next": "Runaway Jim", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2024-08-09", "venue": "Bethel Woods Center for the Arts", "city": "Bethel", "state": "NY", "gap": 5, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "> from \"Tweezer\". If you didn't know any better, you might think the beginning of this jam was out of \"Melt\" and not \"Pillow Jets\". Out of the muck, Trey leads the band into an upbeat, driving jam that oozes energy. Trey weaves his way back to a smooth segue -> \"Tweezer\".", "out": "->", "prev": "Tweezer", "in": ">", "next": "Tweezer", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2024-08-16", "venue": "The Woodlands", "city": "Dover", "state": "DE", "gap": 4, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "> from \"Ruby Waves,\" the jam (once through the song) is more an interlude, a punishing kaleidoscope of sound sure to please shoegazers and those with their heads in the clouds. Terrific outro-cum-drawn-out segue for a rabid \"YPC.\"", "out": "->", "prev": "Ruby Waves", "in": ">", "next": "Your Pet Cat", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2024-08-29", "venue": "Dick's Sporting Goods Park", "city": "Commerce City", "state": "CO", "gap": 3, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Jam takes a sudden and incredibly frenetic turn coming out of the grimy \"Multibeast\" section. The band conjures not just thunder, but a multifaceted visionary journey through shifting sounds and moods as diverse as the Vedic pantheon before settling into a rhythmic and loop laden space that gives way abruptly to \"2001\".", "out": ">", "prev": "Sigma Oasis", "next": "Also Sprach Zarathustra", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2024-12-31", "venue": "Madison Square Garden", "city": "New York", "state": "NY", "gap": 10, "set": "3", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Part of the NYE festivities with additional vocals from the conjurors of thunder, the jam is primarily a moody, dark affair that eventually builds to a crescendo.", "note": "With additional vocals from dancers.", "out": ">", "prev": "Character Zero", "next": "Auld Lang Syne", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2025-04-23", "venue": "Bill Graham Civic Auditorium", "city": "San Francisco", "state": "CA", "gap": 9, "set": "2", "prev": "Crosseyed and Painless", "in": ">", "next": "You Enjoy Myself", "nb": 1},
